# Pairs with RestoredCutNotReAdvanced (issue #4441 F9). The swap runs before
# the fence engaged - a commit re-driven after a crash that skips the engage,
# or a swap ordered before it - so receiving is open and the restored copy is
# not closed when it becomes routable, and a pre-restore write lands on it.
MODULE: RestoredCutNotReAdvancedSwapBeforeEngage
TARGET: RestoredCutNotReAdvanced
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the alias swaps before the fence engaged
PERTURBS: CutoverSwap

--- FIND
    /\ alias[c] = "old"
    /\ "new" \in closed[c]
    /\ alias' = [alias EXCEPT ![c] = "new"]
--- REPLACE
    /\ alias[c] = "old"
    \* MUTATION: no engaged fence required.
    /\ alias' = [alias EXCEPT ![c] = "new"]
--- END